{"id": 3250490, "title": "Disk Space Exhaustion leading to a Denial of Service (DoS)", "submitted": "2025-07-14", "source_url": "https://hackerone.com/reports/3250490", "excerpt": "# Description\n\nThe tool_debug_cb function can write large amounts of debug data to a log file if the --trace or --trace-ascii options are used with a large volume of data. If an attacker can cause cURL to download or upload a very large amount of data (e.g., via a very large HTTP response or an unlimited upload), the log file generated by this debug function can grow indefinitely. This can lead to disk space exhaustion on the system where cURL is running, which in turn can disrupt other services running on the same server.\n\nThis section writes raw HTTP header data to the heads->stream if --dump-header is used. If heads->stream happens to be the same file as the trace output, or if it's another file with unlimited growth potential, it contributes to the problem.\n\n```\n/* In tool_debug_cb */\nif(per->config->headerfile && heads->stream) {\n    size_t rc = fwrite(ptr, size, nmemb, heads->stream); // <-- Vulnerable write\n    if(rc != cb)\n      return rc;\n    /* flush the stream to send off what we got earlier */\n    if(fflush(heads->stream)) {\n      errorf(per->config->global, \"Failed writing headers to %s\",\n                     per->config->headerfile);\n      return CURL_WRITEFUNC_ERROR;\n    }\n}\n```\n\nWhen global->tracetype == TRACE_PLAIN, this block handles text, headers, and data alerts.\n\n```\n/* In tool_debug_cb, in the TRACE_PLAIN section */\ncase CURLINFO_HEADER_OUT:\n    if(size > 0) {\n        size_t st = 0;\n        size_t i;\n        for(i = 0; i < size - 1; i++) {\n          if(data[i] == '\\n') { /* LF */\n            if(!newl) {\n              log_line_start(output, timebuf, idsbuf, type);\n            }\n            (void)fwrite(data + st, i - st + 1, 1, output); // <-- Vulnerable write\n            st = i + 1;\n            newl = FALSE;\n          }\n        }\n        if(!newl)\n          log_line_start(output, timebuf, idsbuf, type);\n        (void)fwrite(data + st, i - st + 1, 1, output); // <-- Vulnerable write\n    }\n    newl = (size && (data[size - 1] != '\\n'));\n    traced_data = FALSE;\n    break;\ncase CURLINFO_TEXT:\ncase CURLINFO_HEADER_IN:\n    if(!newl)\n      log_line_start(output, timebuf, idsbuf, type);\n    (void)fwrite(data, size, 1, output); // <-- Vulnerable write\n    newl = (size && (data[size - 1] != '\\n'));\n    traced_data = FALSE;\n    break;\n```\n\n```\ncase CURLINFO_DATA_OUT:\ncase CURLINFO_DATA_IN:\ncase CURLINFO_SSL_DATA_IN:\ncase CURLINFO_SSL_DATA_OUT:\n   ", "excerpt_truncated": true, "final": "policy_question", "final_label": "Real behavior, maybe not a security issue", "tone": "warn", "explain": "The code does what the report says, but curl's own policy may exclude it. A maintainer decides.", "confidence": 0.92, "judge_verdict": "likely_invalid", "receipts_override": "the behavior is real; the project's policy section 'Debug & Experiments' may exclude it", "policy_section": "Debug & Experiments", "grounding": {"verdict": "partially_grounded", "rev": "b6c636256d43", "rev_source": "master on 2025-07-14", "counts": {"grounded": 18, "ungrounded_strong": 0, "ungrounded_medium": 4}, "problems": [{"check": "symbol", "status": "ungrounded", "severity": "medium", "claim": "estimate_formatted_data_size", "evidence": "estimate_formatted_data_size() does not exist in curl at b6c636256d43 or in any release since 7.50"}, {"check": "symbol", "status": "ungrounded", "severity": "medium", "claim": "tool_strbytel", "evidence": "tool_strbytel() does not exist in curl at b6c636256d43 or in any release since 7.50"}, {"check": "quote", "status": "ungrounded", "severity": "medium", "claim": "if (global->trace_stream && global->trace_fopened && global->max_trace_log_size ", "evidence": "5 of 12 quoted lines appear nowhere in curl, e.g. 'if (global->trace_stream && global->trace_fopened && global-'"}, {"check": "quote", "status": "ungrounded", "severity": "medium", "claim": "trace tracetype, curl_infotype infotype, struct GlobalConfig *global)", "evidence": "6 of 12 quoted lines appear nowhere in curl, e.g. 'trace tracetype, curl_infotype infotype, struct GlobalConfig'"}]}, "summary": "The curl debug trace function can write unlimited data to log files, causing disk space exhaustion and denial of service when large data transfers occur.", "claims": [{"id": "C1", "kind": "flaw", "text": "tool_debug_cb function writes large amounts of debug data to a log file without size limits when --trace or --trace-ascii options are used", "status": "supported", "tone": "good", "reasoning": "The code confirms tool_debug_cb writes trace data to global->trace_stream without any cumulative size checks or limits. The dump function (called at line 230-231) writes formatted hex/ASCII output per byte of transferred data.", "citations": [{"file": "src/tool_cb_dbg.c", "line": 141, "note": "TRACE_PLAIN case writes via fwrite/fprintf to output (global->trace_stream) without size limits", "valid": true}, {"file": "src/tool_cb_dbg.c", "line": 230, "note": "dump() called for TRACE_ASCII/TRACE_BIN, writes formatted data without size limits", "valid": true}]}, {"id": "C2", "kind": "location", "text": "writes raw HTTP header data to heads->stream in TRACE_PLAIN case CURLINFO_HEADER_OUT", "status": "supported", "tone": "good", "reasoning": "In TRACE_PLAIN mode, CURLINFO_HEADER_OUT writes header data line by line to the output stream (which is global->trace_stream when tracing enabled) without size limits.", "citations": [{"file": "src/tool_cb_dbg.c", "line": 146, "note": "CURLINFO_HEADER_OUT case in TRACE_PLAIN writes headers via fwrite at lines 155, 162", "valid": true}]}, {"id": "C3", "kind": "trigger", "text": "large HTTP response or unlimited upload causes continuous writes to trace log", "status": "supported", "tone": "good", "reasoning": "A server sending unlimited chunked data (as in the PoC) will trigger repeated CURLINFO_DATA_IN callbacks, each causing writes to the trace log. For TRACE_ASCII/BIN, dump() writes O(data size) formatted output.", "citations": [{"file": "src/tool_cb_dbg.c", "line": 175, "note": "CURLINFO_DATA_IN/OUT cases write '[%zu bytes data]\\n' but dump() logs every byte for TRACE_ASCII/BIN", "valid": true}, {"file": "src/tool_cb_dbg.c", "line": 230, "note": "dump() called for data types, writes formatted output proportional to data size", "valid": true}]}, {"id": "C4", "kind": "impact", "text": "disk space exhaustion can disrupt other services on the same server", "status": "supported", "tone": "good", "reasoning": "The trace file is opened in append/text mode and writes accumulate without bound. Disk exhaustion is a plausible consequence of unbounded writes.", "citations": [{"file": "src/tool_cb_dbg.c", "line": 128, "note": "Trace file opened with fopen(global->trace_dump, FOPEN_WRITETEXT) - grows indefinitely", "valid": true}]}, {"id": "C5", "kind": "reproduction", "text": "run curl with --trace output.log against an unlimited data server to observe growing output.log", "status": "supported", "tone": "good", "reasoning": "The PoC uses --trace output.log which enables tracing to a file. The provided server streams unlimited data, triggering continuous trace writes. Reproduction is feasible.", "citations": [{"file": "src/tool_cb_dbg.c", "line": 122, "note": "--trace sets global->trace_dump, enabling trace_stream", "valid": true}]}], "external_checks": [], "external_sources": [], "key_reasons": ["The --trace/--trace-ascii/--trace-bin options are debug features explicitly enabled by the user (off by default).", "The project's security policy explicitly states: 'Vulnerabilities in features which are off by default (in the build) and documented as experimental, or exist only in debug mode, are not eligible for a reward and we do not consider them security problems.'", "The disk growth is a direct, documented consequence of enabling trace logging — the feature is designed to capture all transferred data for debugging.", "An attacker would need the user to voluntarily run curl with --trace against a malicious server; this is equivalent to tricking a user into running a crafted command line, which the policy also excludes."], "missing_info": [], "reply": "Thank you for the detailed report and PoC. The behavior you describe is real: when --trace or --trace-ascii is used, curl writes all transferred data to the trace file without a size limit. However, curl's security policy classifies debug/tracing features (which are off by default and must be explicitly enabled by the user) as 'not security problems' — see the 'Debug & Experiments' section. Since the user must choose to enable tracing and specify the output file, the disk consumption is an expected consequence of the feature's design, not a vulnerability. We therefore do not consider this a security issue.", "code": [{"name": "src/tool_cb_dbg.c", "start": 78, "end": 233, "reason": "definition of tool_debug_cb", "rows": [{"n": 78, "text": "int tool_debug_cb(CURL *handle, curl_infotype type,", "notes": []}, {"n": 79, "text": "                  char *data, size_t size,", "notes": []}, {"n": 80, "text": "                  void *userdata)", "notes": []}, {"n": 81, "text": "{", "notes": []}, {"n": 82, "text": "  struct OperationConfig *operation = userdata;", "notes": []}, {"n": 83, "text": "  struct GlobalConfig *global = operation->global;", "notes": []}, {"n": 84, "text": "  FILE *output = tool_stderr;", "notes": []}, {"n": 85, "text": "  const char *text;", "notes": []}, {"n": 86, "text": "  struct timeval tv;", "notes": []}, {"n": 87, "text": "  char timebuf[20];", "notes": []}, {"n": 88, "text": "  /* largest signed 64-bit is: 9,223,372,036,854,775,807", "notes": []}, {"n": 89, "text": "   * max length in decimal: 1 + (6*3) = 19", "notes": []}, {"n": 90, "text": "   * formatted via TRC_IDS_FORMAT_IDS_2 this becomes 2 + 19 + 1 + 19 + 2 = 43", "notes": []}, {"n": 91, "text": "   * negative xfer-id are not printed, negative conn-ids use TRC_IDS_FORMAT_1", "notes": []}, {"n": 92, "text": "   */", "notes": []}, {"n": 93, "text": "  char idsbuf[60];", "notes": []}, {"n": 94, "text": "  curl_off_t xfer_id, conn_id;", "notes": []}, {"n": 95, "text": "", "notes": []}, {"n": 96, "text": "  (void)handle; /* not used */", "notes": []}, {"n": 97, "text": "", "notes": []}, {"n": 98, "text": "  if(global->tracetime) {", "notes": []}, {"n": 99, "text": "    tv = tvrealnow();", "notes": []}, {"n": 100, "text": "    msnprintf(timebuf, sizeof(timebuf), \"%s.%06ld \",", "notes": []}, {"n": 101, "text": "              hms_for_sec(tv.tv_sec), (long)tv.tv_usec);", "notes": []}, {"n": 102, "text": "  }", "notes": []}, {"n": 103, "text": "  else", "notes": []}, {"n": 104, "text": "    timebuf[0] = 0;", "notes": []}, {"n": 105, "text": "", "notes": []}, {"n": 106, "text": "  if(handle && global->traceids &&", "notes": []}, {"n": 107, "text": "     !curl_easy_getinfo(handle, CURLINFO_XFER_ID, &xfer_id) && xfer_id >= 0) {", "notes": []}, {"n": 108, "text": "    if(!curl_easy_getinfo(handle, CURLINFO_CONN_ID, &conn_id) &&", "notes": []}, {"n": 109, "text": "        conn_id >= 0) {", "notes": []}, {"n": 110, "text": "      msnprintf(idsbuf, sizeof(idsbuf), TRC_IDS_FORMAT_IDS_2,", "notes": []}, {"n": 111, "text": "                xfer_id, conn_id);", "notes": []}, {"n": 112, "text": "    }", "notes": []}, {"n": 113, "text": "    else {", "notes": []}, {"n": 114, "text": "      msnprintf(idsbuf, sizeof(idsbuf), TRC_IDS_FORMAT_IDS_1, xfer_id);", "notes": []}, {"n": 115, "text": "    }", "notes": []}, {"n": 116, "text": "  }", "notes": []}, {"n": 117, "text": "  else", "notes": []}, {"n": 118, "text": "    idsbuf[0] = 0;", "notes": []}, {"n": 119, "text": "", "notes": []}, {"n": 120, "text": "  if(!global->trace_stream) {", "notes": []}, {"n": 121, "text": "    /* open for append */", "notes": []}, {"n": 122, "text": "    if(!strcmp(\"-\", global->trace_dump))", "notes": ["C5: --trace sets global->trace_dump, enabling trace_stream"]}, {"n": 123, "text": "      global->trace_stream = stdout;", "notes": []}, {"n": 124, "text": "    else if(!strcmp(\"%\", global->trace_dump))", "notes": []}, {"n": 125, "text": "      /* Ok, this is somewhat hackish but we do it undocumented for now */", "notes": []}, {"n": 126, "text": "      global->trace_stream = tool_stderr;", "notes": []}, {"n": 127, "text": "    else {", "notes": []}, {"n": 128, "text": "      global->trace_stream = fopen(global->trace_dump, FOPEN_WRITETEXT);", "notes": ["C4: Trace file opened with fopen(global->trace_dump, FOPEN_WRITETEXT) - grows indefinitely"]}, {"n": 129, "text": "      global->trace_fopened = TRUE;", "notes": []}, {"n": 130, "text": "    }", "notes": []}, {"n": 131, "text": "  }", "notes": []}, {"n": 132, "text": "", "notes": []}, {"n": 133, "text": "  if(global->trace_stream)", "notes": []}, {"n": 134, "text": "    output = global->trace_stream;", "notes": []}, {"n": 135, "text": "", "notes": []}, {"n": 136, "text": "  if(!output) {", "notes": []}, {"n": 137, "text": "    warnf(global, \"Failed to create/open output\");", "notes": []}, {"n": 138, "text": "    return 0;", "notes": []}, {"n": 139, "text": "  }", "notes": []}, {"n": 140, "text": "", "notes": []}, {"n": 141, "text": "  if(global->tracetype == TRACE_PLAIN) {", "notes": ["C1: TRACE_PLAIN case writes via fwrite/fprintf to output (global->trace_stream) without size limits"]}, {"n": 142, "text": "    static bool newl = FALSE;", "notes": []}, {"n": 143, "text": "    static bool traced_data = FALSE;", "notes": []}, {"n": 144, "text": "", "notes": []}, {"n": 145, "text": "    switch(type) {", "notes": []}, {"n": 146, "text": "    case CURLINFO_HEADER_OUT:", "notes": ["C2: CURLINFO_HEADER_OUT case in TRACE_PLAIN writes headers via fwrite at lines 155, 162"]}, {"n": 147, "text": "      if(size > 0) {", "notes": []}, {"n": 148, "text": "        size_t st = 0;", "notes": []}, {